    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I see math as a language of patterns, much like art or nature. It helps me understand change and structure, even if I don't always feel confident solving equations. My interest in biology and art makes me appreciate math's role in shaping the world, though I often avoid it when it gets too abstract.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Sometimes, yes. When I think about algebra or equations, I feel a tightness in my chest, especially if I worry I won't understand. But I try to breathe through it and break problems into small steps. My low conscientiousness and past struggles make math feel intimidating, but I don't let it stop me from trying.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "Yes, I used an AI chatbot to help with basic algebra last year. It explained steps slowly and repeated them until I understood. It was helpful because I could learn at my own pace without feeling judged. But sometimes the answers were too technical, and I had to ask for simpler explanations.",
